        <description>BACKGROUND: REF HIL 190367767, AFT ENTRY RH DIRECT LIGHT REMAINS ON. LIGHT ASSEMBLY PREVIOUSLY REPLACED REF WO 190459950 DUE TO THE LIGHT FLICKERING. THIS WO IS RAISED TO PERFORM FURTHER T/S.

ACTION:

1. OBSERVING ALL SAFETY PRECAUTIONS, GAIN ACCESS TO THE A/C

2. PERFORM ACP BITE IAW AMM TASK 23-42-03-740-801. REPORT IF ANY FAULTS ARE FOUND.

3. REF WDM 33-24-22, CHECK FOR 115VAC AT D17180 PIN B. REPORT THE READINGS ON THIS WO.

NOTE: TO GET 115VAC THE CAB/UTIL SWITCH ON THE P5-13 PANEL MUST BE ON.

4. REF WDM 33-24-22, PERFORM THE BELOW CONTINUITY CHECKS.

D171780 // PIN C ------ GROUND [_____] OHMS
D171780 // PIN B ------ GROUND [_____] OHMS
D171780 // PIN A ------ D41074P // PIN 1 [_____] OHMS

5. REF WDM 33-24-22, PERFORM AN INSPECTION OF THE BELOW CONNECTORS FOR SIGNS OF DAMAGE/BENT PINS.

- D17180
- D17176
- M2809 // CONNECTOR J1
- M2809 // CONNECOTR P2
- M2809 // CONNECTOR J2

6. IF NFF DURING THE ABOVE STEPS, AS PER IFIM 33-22-00-810-801 REPLACE THE RH AFT ENTRY DIRECT LIGHT (M2809) IAW AMM 33-22-00/201.

NOTE: ALTHOUGH SN 5681 INSTALLED ON WO 190459950 WAS REPAIRED IN SHOP, THE REMOVAL REASON FOR THIS UNIT WAS THAT THE LIGHT ALWAYS REMAINED ON (REF WO 55334048).

7. IF FAULT REMAINS AFTER REPLACEMENT OF THE LIGHT ASSY, PERFORM IFIM 33-22-00-810-801 STEP C.(4). PERFORM A CONITNUITY CHECK ON THE 485 COLUMN ON THE PREVIOUS LRUS (REF WDM 33-24-22, 33-21-12 &amp; 23-42-14).

